+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Make a vector of plate barcodes for each cell</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxucGxhdGUuYmFyY29kZXMgPSBsYXBwbHkoY29sbmFtZXMocmF3LmRhdGEpLCBmdW5jdGlvbih4KSBzdHJzcGxpdChzdHJzcGxpdCh4LCBcIl9cIilbWzFdXVsxXSwgJy4nLCBmaXhlZD1UUlVFKVtbMV1dWzJdKVxuYGBgIn0= -->
+<pre class="r"><code>plate.barcodes = lapply(colnames(raw.data), function(x) strsplit(strsplit(x, &quot;_&quot;)[[1]][1], '.', fixed=TRUE)[[1]][2])</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Make per-cell metadata, and reorder the raw data by plate for consistency. Make a plate barcode dataframe to “expand” the per-plate metadata to be per-cell.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuYmFyY29kZS5kZiA9IHQuZGF0YS5mcmFtZShhcy5kYXRhLmZyYW1lKHBsYXRlLmJhcmNvZGVzKSlcbnJvd25hbWVzKGJhcmNvZGUuZGYpID0gY29sbmFtZXMocmF3LmRhdGEpXG5jb2xuYW1lcyhiYXJjb2RlLmRmKSA9IGMoJ3BsYXRlLmJhcmNvZGUnKVxuaGVhZChiYXJjb2RlLmRmKVxuYGBgIn0= -->
+<pre class="r"><code>barcode.df = t.data.frame(as.data.frame(plate.barcodes))
+rownames(barcode.df) = colnames(raw.data)
+colnames(barcode.df) = c('plate.barcode')
+head(barcode.df)</code></pre>
